; DB connection config consumed by Utils\Connectivity\Database.
;
; Sections are keyed by database name (the section header IS the database
; name), and the connector resolves a database to its [<dbname>] section:
;
;   $conn = Database::connectAs($dbname, $account)
;
; `$account` is a service-account name owned by the consumer (this framework
; does not name any account). The connector reads its password from the
; <ACCOUNT>_PASSWORD key (uppercased account name + `_PASSWORD`); an empty
; value means a passwordless account.
;
; This file carries prod connectivity only, generated per database by
; gen-reuter from etc/machines.ini + etc/deploy.conf. The dev sandbox lives
; in var/sandbox/<name>-<guid>/reuter.ini (generated by 'ema sandbox
; srv/<name>-<GUID>'), not here.
;
; The <ACCOUNT>_PASSWORD keys are consumer-side credentials, written by the
; consumer's own service-user provisioning (ema no longer emits users/grants).
; This framework only reads them; gen-reuter preserves any *_PASSWORD keys it
; finds without naming the accounts.
;
; Transport: the section is authoritative for the 'ema' CLI. When
; MYSQL_UNIX_PORT is set, ema connects via that socket (root/unix_socket
; auth); otherwise it uses SERVER/PORT over TCP. The app layer
; (Utils\Connectivity\Database) reads MYSQL_UNIX_PORT from .env, not from
; this file, so in prod it stays TCP-only (.env is MYSQL_*-free).

[mydb]
SERVER=10.147.x.10
PORT=3307
DBMS=mariadb
; <ACCOUNT>_PASSWORD = ...   (one per consumer service account)
MYSQL_UNIX_PORT=/path/to/mysql.sock
